From: bigjakk <6015188+bigjakk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: kcc: HRTF panner computes azimuth/elevation twice per quantum, not 128x

Stock behaviour (third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/
panner_handler.cc, PannerHandler::ProcessSampleAccurateValues):

PannerHandler::Process takes the sample-accurate path whenever the
panner's or the AudioListener's params have automation
("HasSampleAccurateValues() ||
listener_handler_->HasSampleAccurateValues()") and any of them is
a-rate (the default).  Howler updates the listener with setTargetAtTime
every frame, so the listener always has automation and every PannerNode
in the scene takes this path in every render quantum.  The path fills
azimuth_values_[k], elevation_values_[k] and total_gain_values_[k] for
all 128 frames; each CalculateAzimuthElevation() call is four vector
normalisations, two cross products and two acos.

The two angle arrays have exactly two readers:
 - panner_->PanWithSampleAccurateValues(azimuth, elevation, ...).  For
   the HRTF model (third_party/blink/renderer/platform/audio/
   hrtf_panner.cc) this is "Sample-accurate (a-rate) HRTF panner is not
   implemented, just k-rate" and calls
   Pan(desired_azimuth[0], elevation[0], ...).  EqualPowerPanner reads
   azimuth[i] for every frame.
 - "cached_azimuth_ = azimuth_values_[frames_to_process - 1]" (and the
   same for elevation), used by the non-sample-accurate branch of
   Process() in a later quantum when nothing is dirty.
So with an HRTF panner 126 of the 128 pairs are computed and never read.

Change (feature KccHrtfPannerKRateAngles, disabled by default):

When the feature is on and panning_model_ is kHRTF, the loop calls
CalculateAzimuthElevation() only for k == 0 and
k == frames_to_process - 1.  Everything that is read per frame is left
alone: the panner and listener param arrays are still filled in full
(that is also what advances the AudioParams), and
CalculateDistanceConeGain() still runs for every frame because
CopyWithSampleAccurateGainValuesFrom() applies total_gain_values_ per
frame.  The equal-power model is untouched.

The output is bit-identical to stock: CalculateAzimuthElevation() is a
pure function of its arguments, the two pairs that are read are computed
from the same inputs as before, and the build uses -ffp-contract=off.
The entries in between keep whatever they held (the arrays are zero
initialised on allocation); they are not read while the model is HRTF,
and a switch to equal-power takes effect in a later Process() call,
which refills them in full.

The feature state is read once per PannerHandler in the constructor
(main thread) into a const member, so the audio thread does not query
base::FeatureList.  panning_model_ and panner_ are only changed with
process_lock_ held, and ProcessIfNecessary() holds it around Process().

Listener arrays (AudioListenerHandler::UpdateValuesIfNeeded): looked at,
not changed.  The nine 128-entry arrays are filled once per quantum for
the whole context, not per panner; position is read per frame by the
distance gain; forward/up are then only read at the first and last
frame by HRTF panners, but filling them is CalculateSampleAccurateValues
running the timeline, which also stores the param's end-of-quantum
value, and an equal-power panner in the same graph reads all of them.
There is no provable saving of any size there.

A/B: --enable-features=KccHrtfPannerKRateAngles
 - Identity: render the same graph in an OfflineAudioContext (HRTF
   PannerNodes fed by oscillators or buffers, listener and/or panner
   positions automated with setTargetAtTime / setValueAtTime /
   linearRampToValueAtTime) with and without the flag and compare the
   rendered buffers; they must be equal sample for sample.
 - Cost: wall time of startRendering() for that graph with, say, 64
   HRTF panners and 30 s of audio; or in the game, a trace with
   disabled-by-default-webaudio.audionode and the duration of
   "PannerHandler::Process" slices during a firefight; or audio thread
   CPU.  The gain per panner per quantum is 126 azimuth/elevation
   evaluations.

Platforms: all (no platform-specific code).

Not verified: compilation.

Build and check status (2026-11-21)
  - Compiled without any change on Windows, in the Electron 45.4.1 DCHECK
    build (dcheck_always_on) and in the official Release build (dist.zip).
  - DCHECK build: test/page-check.js + hrtf.html: four renders in
    OfflineAudioContexts (switch off twice, on twice) are identical sample for
    sample (one SHA-256).
  - Release build (dist.zip): the four renders are identical sample for
    sample.
  - Not checked: the CPU saved per quantum (not measured).
The "not compiled" / "not verified" notes above were written before the
build; they stay for the caveats they list. Details and raw logs:
patches/electron-45/RESULTS.md and results/.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.cc
index 1c46560af72fb8bc1f3a5f3948e0a47963b85eac..35b4b17dc76ecceb5c16582134e2d48fe200c85f 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <array>
 
 #include "base/compiler_specific.h"
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/metrics/histogram_functions.h"
 #include "base/numerics/angle_conversions.h"
 #include "base/synchronization/lock.h"
@@ -29,6 +30,18 @@ namespace {
 constexpr unsigned kMinimumOutputChannels = 1;
 constexpr unsigned kMaximumOutputChannels = 2;
 
+// KCC: when enabled, a panner that uses the HRTF model computes the azimuth
+// and elevation only for the frames of a render quantum whose angles are
+// read (the first and the last) instead of for every frame.  See
+// `PannerHandler::ProcessSampleAccurateValues()`.
+BASE_FEATURE(kKccHrtfPannerKRateAngles, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
+bool IsKccHrtfPannerKRateAnglesEnabled() {
+  static const bool enabled =
+      base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kKccHrtfPannerKRateAngles);
+  return enabled;
+}
+
 double EnsureFinite(double x) {
   return std::isfinite(x) ? x : 0.0;
 }
@@ -50,7 +63,8 @@ PannerHandler::PannerHandler(AudioNode& node,
       orientation_x_(&orientation_x),
       orientation_y_(&orientation_y),
       orientation_z_(&orientation_z),
-      listener_handler_(&node.context()->listener()->Handler()) {
+      listener_handler_(&node.context()->listener()->Handler()),
+      kcc_hrtf_k_rate_angles_(IsKccHrtfPannerKRateAnglesEnabled()) {
   AddInput();
   AddOutput(kMaximumOutputChannels);
 
@@ -280,6 +294,17 @@ void PannerHandler::ProcessSampleAccurateValues(AudioBus* destination,
   base::span<const float> up_z =
       listener_handler_->GetUpZValues(render_quantum_frames);
 
+  // KccHrtfPannerKRateAngles: `HRTFPanner::PanWithSampleAccurateValues()` reads
+  // only the first azimuth/elevation pair, and the only other reader of the
+  // two arrays is the update of `cached_azimuth_` and `cached_elevation_`
+  // below, which takes the last pair.  For the HRTF model the pairs in between
+  // are therefore never read and need not be computed.  The distance and cone
+  // gain is applied per frame and is always computed.  `panning_model_` and
+  // `panner_` only change with `process_lock_` held, and
+  // `ProcessIfNecessary()` holds it around this call.
+  const bool first_and_last_angles_only =
+      kcc_hrtf_k_rate_angles_ && panning_model_ == Panner::PanningModel::kHRTF;
+
   // Compute the azimuth, elevation, and total gains for each position.
   for (unsigned k = 0; k < frames_to_process; ++k) {
     gfx::Point3F panner_position(panner_x_values_[k], panner_y_values_[k],
@@ -291,9 +316,11 @@ void PannerHandler::ProcessSampleAccurateValues(AudioBus* destination,
     gfx::Vector3dF listener_forward(forward_x[k], forward_y[k], forward_z[k]);
     gfx::Vector3dF listener_up(up_x[k], up_y[k], up_z[k]);
 
-    CalculateAzimuthElevation(&azimuth_values_[k], &elevation_values_[k],
-                              panner_position, listener_position,
-                              listener_forward, listener_up);
+    if (!first_and_last_angles_only || k == 0 || k == frames_to_process - 1) {
+      CalculateAzimuthElevation(&azimuth_values_[k], &elevation_values_[k],
+                                panner_position, listener_position,
+                                listener_forward, listener_up);
+    }
 
     total_gain_values_[k] = CalculateDistanceConeGain(
         panner_position, orientation, listener_position);
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.h b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.h
index d0a4747a386b188328666fd82ebc4d0ec9d25ebd..d018f511e67576cf74b39325e728663f02115045 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/panner_handler.h
